      "head_commit": {
        "id": "cd4e50b15d9777860c51b5ca5a33aabbe802c7a6",
        "tree_id": "461d0dc35c69d26a38affc7bc6cc7665d81dde51",
        "message": "fix(19): I put comment lines between backslash continuations — the same trap, again\n\n    .../line 28: -DLLAMA_BUILD_APP=OFF: command not found\n    ##[error]Process completed with exit code 127.\n\nMY OWN FLAG NEVER REACHED CMAKE. The explanation block I added for\nLLAMA_BUILD_APP was inserted INTO the middle of the `cmake` invocation, between\nits continuation lines:\n\n    cmake -S src-llama -B build \\\n      ...\n      -DLLAMA_BUILD_TESTS=OFF ... \\\n      # LLAMA_BUILD_APP IS THE ONE THAT WAS MISSING ...\n      # ...\n      -DLLAMA_BUILD_APP=OFF ...\n\n`\\` + newline joins the next line onto this one, the `#` then comments out the\nrest of the JOINED line, cmake silently never ran, and the flag line became a\ncommand name. Exactly the failure fixed in 5f8e6f1, committed again two commits\nlater, and in the same session that recorded the rule.\n\nTHE FLAG IS ON ONE UNBROKEN CONTINUATION NOW\n\nThe explanation is hoisted ABOVE the `cmake` invocation, where a `#` cannot be\njoined onto a backslash, and the command is verified programmatically rather than\nby eye:\n\n    $ python3 -c \"...parse the YAML, slice the cmake command, assert no '#'\"\n    -DLLAMA_BUILD_APP=OFF -DLLAMA_BUILD_COMMON=OFF -DLLAMA_BUILD_UI=OFF \\\n    -G Ninja\n    --- no comment inside the continuation: OK ---\n\nAND A REPO-WIDE SWEEP FOR THE SHAPE\n\n    $ python3 - <<'PY'   # every workflow and script\n      for i in range(len(L)-1):\n          if L[i].rstrip().endswith('\\\\') and L[i+1].lstrip().startswith('#'): ...\n    PY\n      traps: 0\n\nThis is the third time in this repository that a shell/YAML mechanic has cost\nmore time than the thing it was meant to test, and the first two were found by a\nlinter before commit. The sweep is now part of every change that touches a\nworkflow or a script.\n\nWorth noting from the same log: `-- Generating embedded license file for target:\nllama-app` confirms LLAMA_BUILD_APP was never OFF, which is the failure this was\nmeant to prevent.",
        "timestamp": "2026-09-29T01:20:31Z",
