        "tree_id": "c633371f60a11a44799337f3ba103ff58856c3a3",
        "message": "fix(18): LLAMA_BUILD_APP defaults ON and built a CLI whose deps we had disabled\n\nThe pin took, and it took visibly:\n\n    llama.cpp pinned: 3018a11e79e489b657dbb77c95694889ccff92df\n    header has llama_get_memory\n    header has llama_memory_clear\n    -- ggml commit:  3018a11\n\nSo the 11 API errors are resolved -- the header assertions now pass at configure\ntime instead of the wrapper failing to compile twenty minutes later.\n\nThe first build at the new pin failed differently:\n\n    FAILED: [code=1] bin/llama\n    ld: error: unable to find library -lllama-server-impl\n    ld: error: unable to find library -lllama-cli-impl\n    clang++: error: linker command failed with exit code 1\n\nTHE OPTION THAT WAS MISSING\n\nAt 3018a11e7 the top-level CMakeLists.txt declares:\n\n    option(LLAMA_BUILD_APP \"llama: build the unified binary\" ${LLAMA_STANDALONE})\n\n${LLAMA_STANDALONE} is ON for a standalone build, so LLAMA_BUILD_APP is ON by\ndefault. The flags passed here set TESTS, EXAMPLES and SERVER to OFF but never\nmentioned APP -- so pinning the desktop commit switched on a target the previously\npinned branch did not have. The unified binary links llama-server-impl and\nllama-cli-impl, and EXAMPLES/SERVER being OFF is exactly what removed those, so\nbin/llama was assembled with its own dependencies switched out from under it.\n\nTwo more are ON by default at this commit and equally unnecessary here:\n\n    option(LLAMA_BUILD_COMMON \"llama: build common utils library\" ${LLAMA_STANDALONE})\n    option(LLAMA_BUILD_UI     \"llama: build the embedded Web UI for server\"     ON)\n\nAdded: -DLLAMA_BUILD_APP=OFF -DLLAMA_BUILD_COMMON=OFF -DLLAMA_BUILD_UI=OFF\n\nWHY IT MATTERS BEYOND THE LINK ERROR\n\nbuild.rs links EVERY .a the package ships (crates/gs-ffi/build.rs:200 walks lib/\nand links each stem it finds). So leaving a CLI in dist/lib/ would not merely cost\ndisk -- rustc would be handed it as a link input. The package needs to contain\nlibraries and nothing else.\n\nNothing in this stack wants a CLI, a server, or the common utils: the wrapper\ncalls llama_* and ggml_* APIs only, which is why the only errors it produced were\nabout those two namespaces.",
